Mac Island & Dock 2.0.1 (by caliberda, GPL-3.0): Bluetooth list fixes, published by Glasshouse as "fix3".
Applies to https://mods.windhawk.net/mods/mac-island-dock/2.0.1.wh.cpp (sha256 9434ec71...82d95).

1. A device clicked in the Bluetooth list stayed on "Connecting..." or "Disconnecting..." for good, and every
   other click in the list was ignored: a panel's timers go off once (Panel::HandleMessage kills them first),
   and CheckBluetoothStep never set its timer again, so the device was only looked at after 0.3 s.
2. Disconnect left headphones connected: only the first audio filter holding the device's address was asked.
   Headphones have two (music and headset), and with Intel's Bluetooth audio offload the headset's filter
   doesn't hold the address at all. Now every filter of the device is asked, also those found by the
   device's container ID.

Built with Windhawk's own compiler (clang++ -std=c++23 -O2, the mod's @compilerOptions), 64- and 32-bit.

